    "name": {
      "cards": [
        {
          "text": "That steady tick you tapped is the [[pulse|pulse]]. It is the tick you feel under music, like a clock or a heartbeat. It is what your foot taps to when a song comes on."
        },
        {
          "text": "Each tick of the pulse is one [[beat|beat]]. Tap your foot 4 times and you have tapped 4 beats. Beats are what we count music in."
        },
        {
          "text": "The pulse does not stop for long sounds. If a tune holds one sound for a long time, the ticks carry on underneath it. That is why you can keep tapping your foot all the way through a song."
        }
      ],
      "alternative": {
        "text": "Bounce a ball and listen: bounce, bounce, bounce. Each bounce is one beat, and the gaps between them are all equal. If the ball bounced in an uneven way, it would feel wrong. That even gap is what makes a pulse."
      }
    },
